id: references/interception
title: "Interception — awareness between emotion and action"
kind: public-research-reference
status: public-working-paper
updated: 2026-08-29

coordinate: https://yawn.bot/interception
source_repository: https://github.com/yawn-ai/yawn.bot
source_model: https://yawn.bot/interception/model.yawn
license: CC-BY-4.0
peer_review_status: not-peer-reviewed

principal:
  name: David Forman
  role: principal of @dave

purpose: >
  Hold the public, evidence-bounded reference frame for Interception and make
  the paper's construct, sources, inferences, limitations, and test boundary
  inspectable outside the application repository.

definition: >
  Interception is the moment an activated pattern becomes observable before it
  becomes behavior. Operationally it requires detection, representation, and
  an altered probability of the next action.

call_out: >
  Interception does not stop emotion. It loosens the learned coupling between
  emotion and the next action. Emotion may supply the signal; awareness makes
  the interception.

sequence:
  - Programming
  - Emotion
  - Interception
  - Yawn
  - Choice
  - Update

# Revision-2 conformance (model.yawn revision 2, 2026-08-28): the paper's
# six steps and the ontology's canonical loop are ONE loop at two apertures.
sequence_mapping:
  canonical_loop: >
    Relationship -> Observation -> Relevance -> Orientation -> Intention ->
    Projection -> Consequence -> Proof -> Updated Relationship
  note: >
    Interception is the Observation-becoming-Orientation segment; Projection,
    Consequence, and Proof are carried by the completed-cycle definition.

lacuna:
  id: emotion-action-coupling-untested-as-full-protocol
  statement: >
    Component mechanisms are studied; the complete protocol has never been
    tested against a time-matched neutral pause. This absence is the
    first-class reason the Yawn stays open (Q-int-1..3 carry owners in the
    served model, revision 2, which also splits claim support from
    proof_status so the register can be computed).

connections:
  - ref: core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn
    relation: constitutional-ground
  - ref: yawn.bot yawnalogue contract
    relation: productized-response-gate
  - ref: yawn.bot cognition graduation ladder
    relation: same-ladder-as-claim-proof-status
  - ref: yawn.bot bias-detector operator
    relation: component-mechanism-in-product
  - ref: yawn.bot aperture-router goodhart_guard
    relation: falsifier-guard
  - private_traces: >
      One naturalistic completed-cycle trace exists in the principal's
      private root (2026-08-28); coordinate withheld by the family-privacy
      boundary.

evidence_boundary: >
  No cited study tests Interception as operationally defined. Six cases test
  component mechanisms and two are measurement or engineering analogues.
  Reported results remain distinct from YAWN-specific inference.

case_studies:
  - id: mccurry-conflict-pause-2024
    role: component-mechanism
    paper: https://www.nature.com/articles/s44271-024-00122-4
    open_data: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.12936112
    code: https://github.com/AnnahGrace01/FTF-CRTT
  - id: kircanski-affect-labeling-2012
    role: component-mechanism
    paper: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4721564/
  - id: levy-gigi-labeling-intensity-2022
    role: component-mechanism
    paper: https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0279303
    open_data: https://osf.io/gzjq5/
  - id: mayiwar-self-distancing-2024
    role: component-mechanism
    paper: https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/bdm.2378
    open_data_code_materials: https://osf.io/jhdsf/
  - id: naragon-gainey-decentering-2023
    role: component-mechanism
    paper: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10538949/
    public_project: https://osf.io/gct7x/
  - id: andreu-mindfulness-null-2018
    role: component-mechanism-boundary-null
    paper: https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0191661
    open_data: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1044036
  - id: wager-reappraisal-pathways-2008
    role: mechanism-analogue
    paper: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2742320/
    open_data: https://openneuro.org/datasets/ds000108/versions/00002
  - id: heartsteps-decision-points-2019
    role: engineering-analogue
    paper: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6401341/
    open_data: https://github.com/klasnja/HeartStepsV1

emotional_catalog:
  name: GoEmotions
  role: open-emotion-language-corpus
  sample: 58009 English Reddit comments
  labels: 27 emotions plus neutral
  agreement_filtered_split: 54263
  published_baseline: macro-F1 .46 across 28 labels
  paper: https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.372/
  open_data: https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/goemotions/data
  code: https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/goemotions
  boundary: >
    This is an inspectable vocabulary for expressed English Reddit language,
    not ground truth about private feelings. Platform, culture, filtering, and
    annotation biases apply.

proof:
  source_commit: https://github.com/yawn-ai/yawn.bot/commit/e91798f338fe143b6825d9f5e109c05def239766
  source_pr: https://github.com/yawn-ai/yawn.bot/pull/78
  deployment: dpl_HdYmDromXpyk4QTJvgaSV3txqqGQ
  canonical_http: "200 for /interception and /interception/model.yawn"
  browser: "David Forman, principal of @dave, 29 August 2026, canonical metadata, 9 paper sections, 28 catalog labels, no horizontal overflow, no route-owned console errors"
  status: production-verified

boundary:
  - public working paper, not peer reviewed
  - conceptual and research artifact, not medical advice or therapy
  - awareness is not automatically agency
  - neural change is not behavioral proof
  - labels are provisional models rather than hidden truth
  - no private state, persistence, model call, or runtime mutation
